Example 2: When the Method overridden in one class onlyThe code shows multiple inheritance where Class4 inherits from Class2 and Class3; calling obj.m() executes Class3’s method due to Python’s method resolution order (MRO).
            Python

    class Class1:
    def m(self):
        print("In Class1")

class Class2(Class1):
    pass

class Class3(Class1):
    def m(self):
        print("In Class3")

class Class4(Class2, Class3):
    pass

obj = Class4()
obj.m()

