Example 3: All classes define the same methodThe code demonstrates multiple inheritance, showing that Class4 overrides the m method, but methods from parent classes (Class2, Class3, Class1) can still be called explicitly using the class name.
            Python

    class Class1:
    def m(self):
        print("In Class1")

class Class2(Class1):
    def m(self):
        print("In Class2")

class Class3(Class1):
    def m(self):
        print("In Class3")

class Class4(Class2, Class3):
    def m(self):
        print("In Class4")

obj = Class4()
obj.m()
Class2.m(obj)
Class3.m(obj)
Class1.m(obj)

